Theorem RL-29: LLVM noalias under preserves_freshness AND Unique

  Preconditions:
    - RL-29 governs noalias export per Annex E §AIMS AIMS -> LLVM Fact
      Export: "Fresh allocation returns (ReturnContract.preserves_freshness =
      true AND ReturnContract.uniqueness = Unique) SHALL be marked LLVM
      noalias. Gate = preserves_freshness, NOT uniqueness alone — a Unique
      parameter passthrough may alias the caller's copy."
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - This is a refinement of the IC-4 ReturnContract: the noalias attribute
      is sound iff the contract proves the return is freshly allocated.
    - depends-on sec-06: IC-4 ReturnContract.preserves_freshness +
      .uniqueness; VF-2 (c) validates noalias against the ReturnContract.

  Soundness property:
    Forall function return value r with ReturnContract (preserves_freshness,
    uniqueness):

      (P1) Emission decision: RL-29 marks r noalias iff preserves_freshness =
           true AND uniqueness = Unique.

      (P2) Soundness (refinement of IC-4): preserves_freshness proves r is
           produced by a fresh allocation (or a callee whose return contract
           also preserves freshness), so the returned pointer aliases NOTHING
           the caller already holds — the noalias attribute is sound. A
           Unique-but-not-fresh return (a parameter passthrough) may alias the
           caller's copy, so uniqueness alone is INSUFFICIENT — the
           preserves_freshness gate is load-bearing.

    RL-29 refines plain ARC (which marks nothing noalias) by exporting the
    AIMS freshness proof to LLVM as a noalias fact the optimizer exploits.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the refinement engine via definitional rewriting
    of the noalias condition against the IC-4 ReturnContract.

    Part (P1/P2) — noalias-emission grid:
      fresh_unique_noalias -> noalias
      unique_not_fresh_no_noalias -> NO noalias (passthrough may alias)
      fresh_maybeshared_no_noalias -> NO noalias
      Coverage gate: 3 decisions. Negative-direction witness: a
      Unique-but-not-fresh (passthrough) return must NOT be marked noalias —
      asserted (the load-bearing preserves_freshness distinction).

    Engines dispatched:
      refinement (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl29_noalias_fresh_unique;
        noalias-condition refinement against IC-4; emits Fail on an unsound
        noalias emission)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      case_analysis (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 refinement engine discharges RL-29 via the noalias-emission gate (preserves_freshness AND Unique) refined against the IC-4 ReturnContract, with a negative-direction witness confirming uniqueness alone is insufficient (a Unique-but-not-fresh passthrough may alias the caller's copy)
